fix(pin-only): count pinned occurrences rather than matching action names

The first version of the depin check intersected action names: an action
SHA pinned on a removed line and loosely referenced on an added line was
reported as depinned. One file may use the same action twice, and a diff that
bumps the pinned occurrence SHA to SHA while bumping an unpinned second
occurrence v7 to v8 puts that action on both sides of that intersection
although nothing was depinned.

What matters is whether the action ends the diff with fewer commit SHA pins
than it started with, so that is what is compared now. Unchanged occurrences
appear on neither side of a diff and cannot affect the counts.

Both directions are covered by tests: two occurrences bumped different ways
is accepted, and two pinned occurrences where one loses its SHA is still
refused. Reproducing the old set intersection exactly makes the first of
those fail and nothing else, which is what says the test is measuring this
and not something adjacent.

